  "rust_authorities": "Rust now owns verified-account bearer admission/rotation/revocation/expiry and bounded social/countdown budgets, plus accepted clan schema, membership, invitations, role/lifecycle gates, public views, request quotas/replay and transactional SQL. Bounded directory continuations bind the actual native account capability and queue source, rechecking revocation and fresh expiry after IO. SQL failure rolls back membership, invitations and replay; retry commits once. Existing original manual/client role evidence remains separate from modern replacement-service implementation. Trusted provider verification, canonical identity/friend/presence/Steam IO, general endpoint limits/readers, complete Rust service replacement, cross-store recovery and original/native played/delivered gates remain open.",
  "reproduced_gap": {
    "trigger": "An internal Python account-session map insertion is presented to the actual authenticated clan HTTP endpoint.",
    "before": "The previous authoritative Python bank accepts an otherwise unadmitted bearer and returns200.",
    "after": "Rust owns bearer admission; immutable Python snapshots cannot authorize a new bearer and the actual HTTP endpoint returns401.",
    "boundary": "Adapter/authority ownership control, not a claimed remote unauthenticated exploit or recovered Xbox Live procedure."
  },
  "checks": [
    "Native account capacity and preflight before canonical identity/history writes; bounded permits and entropy; generation/identity/expiry/rotation/revocation fences",
    "Independent monotonic authentication/rate clocks and separate social/countdown budgets",
    "Read-only account projections and native account-source binding across every SQL/provider continuation, including expiry after IO without another authentication request",
    "One clan per player,100 member cap, exact documented role permissions, confirmed Overlord promotion without automatic demotion, sole-Overlord leave guard and last-member deletion",
    "Authenticated invitations/accept/decline/block/cancel, roster/presence/outgoing visibility, bounded messages/logs and request replay",
    "Actual clan SQL-trigger rollback and exactly-once retry; stale Python role aliases cannot grant authority; native active-clan-match gate and consent invalidation",
    "Full frozen backend and production ABI regressions, plus offline CMake Rust static/CXX/FFI build/helper"
  ],
